From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:12:45 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] AROS: build FlightGear against AROS's C library and
 bsdsocket.library

- sqlite3 (bundled, thread-safe): adapted the way AROS's own sqlite port
  is: no write-ahead log (no shared memory files), the "unix-none" VFS
  first, "Volume:" paths, arc4random_buf() for randomness; exec/types.h
  is read before sqlite defines its own GLOBAL.
- hts_engine: fpos_t is an integer type.
- fgrcc: a cross build takes the resource compiler from FGRCC_EXECUTABLE
  (built for the build machine) instead of building one it cannot run.
- bootstrap: no execinfo.h backtrace handler.
- mongoose: no dlfcn.h, no CGI (no fork()); sockets are closed and set
  non-blocking through the port's support library (libfgaros.a), as a
  socket is not a C library file descriptor.
- JSBSim FGfdmSocket: the same for its sockets.
- fg_os_osgviewer: a static build registers the plugins FlightGear's
  OpenSceneGraph is built with (dds, rgb, jpeg, png, freetype, 3ds, ac,
  osg, txf) and the serializers.

Compiles and links (fgfs) with the pc-x86_64 cross toolchain
(GCC 15.2.0). Not run on AROS yet.
